From 3f42df37fd9bb7eb61094c493fc5a6e49758576e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: kebab bring-up <local@invalid>
Date: Fri, 18 Sep 2026 12:51:01 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] kebab: revert the 0079 imx471 temporary bus scan

0079 has now been run three times under progressively corrected
conditions and has given its answer:

  VANA fixed (0077), 1MHz bus      -> 0x50, 0x58 ACK. Sensor silent.
  VANA fixed, 400kHz bus (0078)    -> 0x50, 0x58 ACK. Sensor silent.
  VANA fixed, 400kHz, VDIG 1.104V  -> 0x50, 0x58 ACK. Sensor silent.
    (0080)

The intervening 1.1V attempt is excluded: it broke the pm8008 regulator
probe outright and unpowered the whole bus, so its all-timeout result
carries no information.

Every controllable variable now matches the vendor description of this
board and each has been verified on the running system rather than
assumed: VANA polarity and actual assertion, reset polarity and actual
release, MCLK4 rate and pin mux, CCI controller clock, CCI bus rate, and
cam_vio / cam_vdig voltages. Under all of them the sensor does not
acknowledge its address anywhere in 0x08-0x77, while the module EEPROM
on the same logical bus answers every time.

Drop the diagnostic. Keep 0077, 0078 and 0080, which are correctness
fixes on their own merits independent of the camera outcome.
---
 drivers/media/i2c/imx471.c | 23 -----------------------
 1 file changed, 23 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/media/i2c/imx471.c b/drivers/media/i2c/imx471.c
index 4f48f75b6..8cca49580 100644
--- a/drivers/media/i2c/imx471.c
+++ b/drivers/media/i2c/imx471.c
@@ -576,29 +576,6 @@ static int imx471_power_on(struct device *dev)
 	 * app doesn't stall for 3s once the hardware is sorted. */
 	usleep_range(50000, 60000);
 
-	/* TEMP DIAGNOSTIC (0075, remove once camera works): the 0070 scan
-	 * above ran while the CCI1 clock was still misconfigured at 19.2MHz
-	 * instead of the 37.5MHz the CCI v2 timing table assumes (fixed in
-	 * patch 0072) -- so that scan's silence is not trustworthy evidence
-	 * of a dead bus. Redo it now, fully powered/clocked/reset-released,
-	 * with the corrected clock rate, and log every address that ACKs. */
-	{
-		struct i2c_client *client = to_i2c_client(dev);
-		struct i2c_adapter *adap = client->adapter;
-		int addr;
-
-		dev_info(dev, "imx471 TEMP DIAG (0075): full bus scan while powered, corrected clock\n");
-		for (addr = 0x08; addr <= 0x77; addr++) {
-			union i2c_smbus_data data;
-			int scan_ret = i2c_smbus_xfer(adap, addr, 0,
-						      I2C_SMBUS_READ, 0,
-						      I2C_SMBUS_BYTE, &data);
-			if (scan_ret >= 0)
-				dev_info(dev, "imx471 TEMP DIAG (0075): addr 0x%02x ACKED\n", addr);
-		}
-		dev_info(dev, "imx471 TEMP DIAG (0075): scan complete\n");
-	}
-
 	return 0;
 }
 
